## Decision drivers

- Accuracy against gold labels on the `test` split must meet or beat the task's quality bar (set in `route.yaml`, decided on `calib`).
- Cost per 1,000 tasks: cloud as measured; local fully loaded (amortised hardware plus energy) at this task's own monthly volume, dedicated scenario.
- The break-even volume must fall at or below this task's monthly volume, and at or below this machine's sustained capacity.
- Tasks listed in `data_must_stay_local` never consider cloud cost or the cloud bar at all: only whether a local candidate meets the bar.

## Options considered

For every task: the local models, the cloud models (one per lineup role), and the applicable non-LLM baseline (TF-IDF for classification, regex for PII redaction, rapidfuzz for entity matching), all measured with the same prompt template, the same lenient parser and the same gold labels.

